      "id": "white",
      "name": "Qular",
      "description": "Nearly the whole horse goes white, and what is left of the coat reads as panels laid on top of it rather than as gaps cut out - big irregular polygons three to ten inches across, scattered over the neck, shoulder, ribcage, barrel, hindquarter and upper legs, and following the muscle as they go. The head is mostly white with panels round the eyes and muzzle; the lower legs often keep a dark boot. How crisp the panel edges are varies a great deal from horse to horse, from soft and feathered to graphic. The mane and tail are not touched by any of it.",
